LUNAR V1.0 — November 15, 2026

Technical derivative of Lunar Navigator, daniel27-space and contributors:
https://github.com/daniel27-space/lunar-navigator
Apache License 2.0; full license in LICENSE and LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

Retained technical foundation: Three.js terrain/globe/shadow implementation,
camera controls, browser ephemeris/horizon/disc/window/finder/landing algorithms,
scientific terrain data preparation and original regression fixtures.
No endorsement or affiliation with the upstream team is implied.

LUNAR modifications: original product interface and guide, Basic/Advanced,
original SVG bearings, base-layout screening, project handling, scientific
workspace, native global DEM input, adjustable shadow fill, WebGL fallback,
Python eclipse model, validation audit, launch/build/release tools and docs.
Modified upstream files retain notices; additional source paths are listed in
qa/upstream_changes.json. Original LUNAR archives remain separate from new work.

Non-NASA welcome/mission artwork, screenshots, promotional narratives and
spacecraft showcases are not used by the V1 application. NASA-origin terrain
and imagery retain their credits in their metadata. Original upstream docs are
preserved under upstream-docs and upstream-pipeline for attribution/provenance.

LUNAR 1.1-preview.1 modifications: original connected-base engineering model, worker search, project workflows, map editing, RF screening, eclipse overlap integration, observer-centred measured-terrain remesh, original educational notes and related checks. The attributed rendering/geometry foundation remains under its existing license. AI-assisted development disclosure remains in README.

LUNAR V1.2 modifications (2026-11-15): adaptive mesh sampling, import recovery, original contextual education and guided Base interface. NASA Apollo photos and source/credit hashes: frontend/public/lunar/history/credits.json.

